# The transaction-intake circuit breaker (App\Services\CircuitBreaker) is
# backed by real Redis (see tsms.circuit_breaker in config/tsms.php) and its
# state is NOT reset between tests (state_ttl_seconds defaults to 3600s).
# Left at the production default of "true", any single full-suite run that
# drives enough genuine 5xx responses through /transactions/official or
# /transactions/batch (e.g. StoreOfficialResilienceTest, which deliberately
# throws mid-persist) trips the breaker open in real Redis, and that "open"
# state then leaks into every other test in the same run that hits those
# routes — even tests with no relationship to circuit-breaker behavior —
# causing false 503 "Circuit is open due to multiple failures" responses.
# Default it off here; tests that specifically exercise circuit-breaker
# behavior opt back in explicitly via config()->set('tsms.circuit_breaker.enabled', true)
# in their own setUp() (see tests/Unit/Services/CircuitBreakerTest.php,
# tests/Unit/Services/TransactionIngestServiceCircuitBreakerTest.php,
# tests/Feature/IngestionCircuitBreakerTest.php), all of which also fake
# Redis via Tests\Traits\FakesCircuitBreakerRedis so they never touch the
# real shared instance.
TSMS_CIRCUIT_BREAKER_ENABLED=false
